tokJitT -- F-123, JITTED Token ON AN INPUT IT CANNOT START (2026-09-24). Token's generated body is
return QuotE() || NumbeR() || StringXP() || TokenXP() || Operators(); and Operators is a bin that carries a generated
parse but is not isRule (isRule 0, hasNewParse 1, binType 4). runOP's term call-through under jitting covered only
isRule, so Operators fell to the isMethod arm and was PARSED AT EMIT TIME: it left no value, the OR degraded (count 1,
"AND/OR RIGHT operand produced no value") and still closed, reading TRUE at consumed 0. ExpressioN's Token+ then ran
to max (100 fires; parseLoop has no no-progress stop), and in the one-process sweep the same fire was exit 139.

The fix widens the jitting arm to hasNewParse; interpreted dispatch is unchanged, so the call-through runs the same
isMethod arm at run time that the interpreted road runs.

Controls first (the three inputs Token can start), then the two subjects, each jitted TWICE (the jitted fire must
hold on the second call) against interpreted. pop.sh asserts every pair agrees on every field, the subjects' values
(% accepts 1 of 1, : bb cc rejects at 0), fires 1, and every compile at degrade 0. H7, measured at landing: with the
arm back at isRule alone, % reads JITTED consumed 0 fires 100 and : bb cc reads JITTED verdict 1.
